      "review_status": "needs_review",
      "review_notes": "Kept as one card because the section describes one local closed process: transaction monitoring controls generate or receive alerts, then those alerts are reviewed for explainability or potential suspiciousness. Manual and automated alerting are alternative ways to produce the same alert output, not separate workflows. Thresholds, customer-profile parameters, scenarios, and account-type differences are represented as standards/inputs used by monitoring rather than chronological stages. Functional_dependency edges only connect the structural entry and local review outcomes; they do not convert parallel standards into a time sequence. AI-based and rules-based systems are treated as context and are not modeled as a separate executable flow because the section does not specify a review workflow for choosing or operating those technologies."
